🤖 Agent: Batch Moscow Mule — serves ~12

Ingredients
- 750 ml vodka (one standard bottle)
- 180 ml fresh lime juice (about 12 medium limes)
- 1.8 L ginger beer (chilled)
- Ice
- 12 lime wheels (for garnish)
- 12 mint sprigs (optional garnish)

Method
1. Chill your ginger beer and vodka ahead of time.
2. In a large pitcher or beverage dispenser, combine the vodka and fresh lime juice. Stir to mix.
3. Just before serving, add the chilled ginger beer and gently stir once to combine (don’t over-stir or you’ll lose fizz).
4. Fill glasses with ice, pour the cocktail, and garnish each with a lime wheel and a mint sprig.

Make-ahead tip: Mix vodka + lime juice up to 24 hours in advance and keep refrigerated; add ginger beer right before the event.
